# Prices, why they fell, caravans, and more everyday work (Docs/Design/62-talk.md, phase 7; the work theme): broad
# scenes nearly any two can have when the topic comes up. topic.what is "a meal" or "herbs" for prices (so "the price
# of #topic.what#" reads right), the good itself for a fall's cause ("timber", "meals"); topic.who is a name or a look;
# topic.where is the other town of a caravan.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Prices up

scene w7c_up_purse
when topic=prices topic.dir=up
a : I took #topic.price# to market and came home with change of nothing. | Have you priced #topic.what# lately? Don't. | My purse is lighter and my basket's lighter. How's that work?
b[wealth=rich] : Is it so much? I suppose it is, for some. | I'll take your word for it. | Magic, I expect.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : I didn't take anything. I hadn't anything to take. | I don't price. I look and walk on. | Mine's been light all year.
b[role=merchant] : Don't look at me. I only pass it on. | Somebody upstream's greedy. Not me. | Costs, #address#. Everyone's costs.
b : Same here. | I have. I wept. | It's a riddle.
a : It's not right. | Wept, and paid. | A cruel one.

scene w7c_up_blame
when topic=prices topic.dir=up
a : Whose fault is it, then? #topic.price# for #topic.what#. | Somebody's getting rich off #topic.what#, and it isn't me. | They say it's the roads. They always say it's the roads.
b[temper=short] : The Houses. It's always the Houses. | Find them and I'll tell them. | Then fix the roads!
b[honesty=sly] : Me. I've been buying it all up. Ha. | Not me. Well. A little me. | It's the roads. Mostly.
b[stage=old] : It was the weather in my day. Now it's the roads. | Nobody's fault. Everybody's fault. | They said it then, too.
b : The carters, I heard. | Someone, somewhere. | And they're right, sometimes.
a : Carters, Houses, the moon. | Somewhere far from here. | Sometimes.

scene w7c_up_cut_back
when topic=prices topic.dir=up
a : We'll be cutting back this week. | No more #topic.what# till it drops. | I'll have to choose: #topic.what#, or boots.
b[parent=yes] : The pups don't understand cutting back. | We've cut back so far there's no back left. | Mine need both.
b[warmth=warm] : Come and eat with us one night. | I'll share mine. No, I insist. | Boots. Then come to me for #topic.what#.
b : Wise. | Good luck to you. | Boots last longer.
a : Needs must. | And to you. | Boots, then.

scene w7c_up_story
when topic=prices topic.dir=up
a : I asked for #topic.what# and the stallholder laughed when I counted out my coin. | A wolf ahead of me at the stall just turned round and left. | I heard someone haggle for #topic.what# for half an hour.
b[humour=merry] : Laughed? Laugh back louder. | Wise wolf. I'll follow them. | Did they win?
b[warmth=warm] : That's cruel. I'd not stand for it. | Poor soul. | Good for them. Somebody has to.
b : The cheek of it. | Can't blame them. | And?
a : I laughed too. Then I left. | Nor me. | They saved a penny. Lost the morning.

scene w7c_up_market_talk
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.place=market
a : #topic.price#. Look at the board. #topic.price#! | Every stall's put #topic.what# up the same. Funny, that. | Shall we buy now, or wait for worse?
b[role=merchant] : Don't shout it. You'll scare the buyers. | Not mine. Mine's honest. Slightly. | Buy now. Tomorrow's dearer.
b : I see it. I wish I didn't. | Not so funny. | Wait. It can't get worse.
a : It can. It always can. | Somebody's talking to somebody. | Can't it?

scene w7c_up_tavern
when topic=prices topic.dir=up here.place=tavern
a : At #topic.price#, I'll be drinking slower. | Cheers to dear #topic.what#. | Everything's going up but my #wages#.
b[humour=dry] : Slower drinking. Longer evenings. Every cloud. | Cheers. To our empty purses. | Your #wages# and the river in summer.
b : Drink up while you can. | Cheers. | Ain't that the way.
a : I intend to. | Cheers. | Every week.

scene w7c_up_meal
when topic=prices topic.item=meal topic.dir=up
a : #topic.price# for a bowl of stew. A bowl! | The pie-wife wants #topic.price# a pie now. | Last week a meal was cheaper. I counted.
b[job=cook|innkeeper] : And the onions cost me double. Someone has to pay. | Flour's dear. Pies are flour. | Not my doing. I'm losing on it.
b[stage=young] : Can we still have pie? | Is pie a lot of #money#? | Can I have half a pie?
b : Cook at home, then. | Bake your own. | You counted?
a : On what fire? | With what flour? | Every penny.

scene w7c_up_herbs
when topic=prices topic.item=herbs topic.dir=up
a : Herbs at #topic.price#. A cough's a luxury now. | I'll not be ill this month. Can't afford it. | They want #topic.price# for a twist of willow bark.
b[job=healer] : I know. I'm paying it too. Come to me if it's bad. | Don't wait till it's bad. Bad's dearer. | Bark grows by the river, free. Take a knife.
b[stage=old] : My knees cost #topic.price# a week now. | Neither will I. I'll lie about it. | I remember it growing on every bank.
b : Gather your own. | Wise. | It's robbery.
a : I don't know which is which. | Very. | Robbery.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Prices down

scene w7c_down_glad
when topic=prices topic.dir=down
a : #topic.what.capitalize#, #topic.price#! Down! | Something got cheaper. Write down the day. | Good news for the purse. Prices are down.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Gods be thanked. I can eat. | Down? I'll believe it. | My purse needs it.
b[role=merchant] : Good for you. Not for me. | I'm writing it. With tears. | Not for the seller's.
b[stage=old] : Won't last. Buy now. | I'll remember it. Won't be many. | Down till Restday, maybe.
b : About time. | Marvellous. | Good.
a : Hurry, then. | It's a rare day. | Very good.

scene w7c_down_why
when topic=prices topic.dir=down
a : Why's #topic.what# cheaper? What's wrong with it? | Down to #topic.price#. Somebody's flooding the market. | Cheap. I don't trust cheap.
b[honesty=guarded] : Nothing's cheap for nothing. Look for the worm. | Somebody's dumping. Wait and see who. | Nor me.
b[humour=merry] : Maybe someone was nice. It happens! Rarely. | Floods are lovely if you've a bucket. | Trust it long enough to buy some.
b : A good harvest, I heard. | Carts came in, I think. | Cheap's cheap.
a : I hope you're right. | Maybe. | Cheap's cheap.

scene w7c_down_stock
when topic=prices topic.dir=down a.stage=adult|old
a : I'll stock up while it's #topic.price#. | Buy now and keep it, that's what my mother did. | Cheap #topic.what#. I'll have the cellar full.
b[drive=ambitious] : Buy it all. Sell it back at the turn. | Your mother was clever. | Fill two.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : With what? | Mine did too, when we had a cellar. | What cellar?
b : Good thinking. | Wise woman. | Don't let it spoil.
a : I'll try. | She was. | I won't.

scene w7c_down_meal
when topic=prices topic.item=meal topic.dir=down
a : A hot meal for #topic.price#. I'll eat out tonight! | Pie's cheaper. Pie's cheaper! | Supper's on me. At these prices.
b[job=cook|innkeeper] : And who's paying the cook? | Cheaper for you. Thinner for me. | Come to mine. I'm matching it.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : I'll have two. | Pie! | I'll hold you to it.
b : Treat yourself. | Pie. Lovely. | Generous.
a : I will. | Pie! | It's cheap.

scene w7c_down_herbs
when topic=prices topic.item=herbs topic.dir=down
a : Herbs are down. My chest'll thank me. | Cheap herbs! I'll buy for the whole winter. | Willow bark at #topic.price#. Glory be.
b[job=healer] : Good. Come and get the right ones. Not the wrong ones. | Dry them well, or they'll rot. | Now folk might come before it's too late.
b : Good. | Clever. | At last.
a : I will. | I'll dry them. | At last.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Why it fell

scene w7c_cause_grateful
when topic=price_cause
a : We've #topic.who# to thank for cheaper #topic.what#. | #topic.who# brought #topic.what# in, and down it came. | You know why #topic.what#'s cheap? #topic.who#.
b[role=merchant] : Thank them? They've cut my margin to the bone. | And down came my profits. | I know. I'm not pleased.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Bless them. Truly. | Bless whoever it was. | Bless them, then.
b[honesty=guarded] : Where'd they get it, though? | Brought it from where? | Hm. I'd ask questions.
b : Well! Good of them. | Lucky us. | Is that so.
a : It was. | Very lucky. | That's so.

scene w7c_cause_who
when topic=price_cause topic.known=no
a : A stranger, #topic.who#, came with #topic.what#. | Some traveller sold the shops #topic.what#. #topic.who#, it was. | Did you see #topic.who#? Brought a load of #topic.what#.
b[stage=young] : Are they still here? Can I see? | Was it a pirate? | I saw them! I think.
b[temper=nervy] : Strangers. I don't like strangers. | What else did they bring? | I'll keep my door locked.
b : Never seen them. | Who's that, then? | I missed them.
a : Passing through, I think. | Nobody knows. | You did.

scene w7c_cause_named
when topic=price_cause topic.known=yes
a : #topic.who# did the town a good turn. #topic.what.capitalize#, cheap. | That #topic.who#'s been bringing #topic.what# in. | Prices fell, and it's #topic.who# did it.
b[pair.band=friends|family] : I always liked them. | Good. They need the trade. | Did they? Good for them.
b : Good of them. | Has she? Has he? | So I heard.
a : Very good. | Loads of it. | So you did.

scene w7c_cause_more
when topic=price_cause
a : Let's hope they bring more #topic.what#. | I'd pay #topic.who# to come again. | If #topic.who# comes back, prices'll fall again.
b[role=merchant] : Let's hope they don't. | I'd pay them to stay away. | Then I'll shut my stall.
b : I'll drink to that. | Me too. | Here's hoping.
a : So will I. | Pay them, then. | Hoping.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Caravans arrived

scene w7c_cv_in_noise
when topic=caravan topic.kind=arrived
a : The #topic.where# wagons rolled in. Woke the whole street. | Mules braying since dawn. #topic.where# carts. | You hear them? #topic.where# caravan's in.
b[tired=yes] : I heard. Every wheel. | Mules. I hate mules. | Heard them? I dreamed them.
b[role=merchant] : Lovely sound. Lovely, lovely sound. | Bless those mules. | Music.
b : Worth the noise. | Mules always bray. | I did.
a : Maybe. | Always. | Who didn't?

scene w7c_cv_in_goods
when topic=caravan topic.kind=arrived
a : What've they brought from #topic.where#, do you know? | There's cloth on the #topic.where# carts. Good cloth. | Salt fish from #topic.where#, I hope.
b[role=merchant] : My order, gods willing. | I'll have it on my stall by noon. | Hope away. I've bought it all.
b[stage=young] : Sweets? Are there sweets? | Can I have a ribbon? | Fish. Yuck.
b : Everything and nothing. | Good. | Fish!
a : Everything, then. | Very. | Fish.

scene w7c_cv_in_news
when topic=caravan topic.kind=arrived
a : The drivers say the road from #topic.where# was quiet. | Carters from #topic.where# have news. | The #topic.where# lot say prices are worse there.
b[temper=nervy] : Quiet? Truly? | Good news, I hope. | Worse? How?
b : Good. | What news? | Can't be.
a : Truly. | Weddings and weather. | It can.

scene w7c_cv_in_carters
when topic=caravan topic.kind=arrived
a : Those carters'll drink the inn dry tonight. | Look at them. Dust from ears to tail. | Poor beasts. They look half dead.
b[job=innkeeper] : Let them. They pay. | I'll have the water hot. | So do the drivers.
b[job=carter] : We earn it. | You'd be dusty too. | That road does it.
b : Let them. | Long road. | Rest them.
a : They will. | Long. | Rest them all.

## Caravans left

scene w7c_cv_out_wave
when topic=caravan topic.kind=left
a : The #topic.where# wagons pulled out at dawn. | Saw the #topic.where# carts off. Long way. | That's the caravan gone for #topic.where#.
b[pair.band=family|spouses] : I hope your cousin's safe on it. | Long way for anyone. | Safe road.
b[role=merchant] : My goods on it, too. | I'll not sleep till they're back. | With my coin.
b : Safe road to them. | Long way. | Good.
a : Safe road. | Long. | Good.

scene w7c_cv_out_quiet
when topic=caravan topic.kind=left
a : Town's quiet with the caravan gone. | No carters in the inn tonight. | Streets are empty without the wagons.
b[job=innkeeper] : Quiet and poor. | No carters, no coin. | Empty, and my till too.
b : Nice, for a change. | Quieter. | I like it.
a : For a change. | Much. | It's nice.

## Caravans raided

scene w7c_cv_raid_who
when topic=caravan topic.kind=raided
a : Raided on the #topic.where# road. Do they know who? | Who'd rob a caravan from #topic.where#? Desperate wolves. | The #topic.where# caravan's lost. Bandits.
b[role=guard] : We've an idea. Not enough of us to act on it. | Desperate, and armed. | Lost, and we were told too late.
b[stage=old] : There's always someone. | Hungry ones. | It's always the same.
b : Nobody knows. | Bandits. | Terrible.
a : Nobody does. | Desperate. | Terrible.

scene w7c_cv_raid_prices
when topic=caravan topic.kind=raided
a : Prices will jump now. Mark me. | No goods from #topic.where# for a month, I'd bet. | Everything dear again, all because of a few thieves.
b[role=merchant] : They already have. I put mine up this morning. | A month? Two. | A few thieves and a lazy Watch.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : We'll go hungry, then. | Can't afford it anyway. | Thieves rob all of us.
b : I fear you're right. | Two, more like. | Aye.
a : I'm always right. | Two. | Aye.

scene w7c_cv_raid_fear
when topic=caravan topic.kind=raided
a : I've a cousin who drives that road. | Do you think they'll come here? | I'll not travel this season.
b[warmth=warm] : Is your cousin all right? Have you heard? | No. Not with the Watch at the gate. | Stay home. Safe.
b[temper=short] : Then your cousin should've stayed home. | Let them try. | Coward.
b : I hope he's all right. | Never. | Nor me.
a : So do I. | I hope. | Nor me.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- More everyday work, for anyone

scene w7c_early_bird
when topic=work
a : I was here before the cock. | First in, every day. Nobody notices. | Who opened up? I thought I'd be first.
b[humour=dry] : The cock's lazy. | I notice. I don't care, but I notice. | A ghost. A very punctual ghost.
b[drive=ambitious] : Second. I'll beat you tomorrow. | Somebody does. Somebody important. | Me. I'm always first.
b : Well done. | I notice. | Me, I think.
a : Thank you. | Do you? | You!

scene w7c_counting
when topic=work
a : Seven, eight... Don't talk, I'm counting. | Lost count. Thanks. | Count it for me, would you? My head's soup.
b[humour=merry] : Twelve, nine, forty... | You're welcome. | Nine. It's always nine.
b[honesty=sly] : I'll count. Trust me. | Sorry. Nine. | I'll keep a few for my trouble.
b : Sorry. | Start again. | Give it here.
a : Hush. | From one. | Thank you.

scene w7c_heavy
when topic=work
a : This is heavier than it looks. | Who packed this? A bear? | My back's gone. Somewhere. I'll find it later.
b[stage=old] : Lift with your legs. I learnt too late. | A careless bear. | Mine went years ago.
b[warmth=warm] : Let me take an end. | Here, together. | Sit. I'll do it.
b : Everything is. | Some fool. | Go easy.
a : Ha. | Some fool. | I'll try.

scene w7c_sharpen
when topic=work
a : Can I use your whetstone? | My blade's dull as a sermon. | Who's had my good knife? It's chipped.
b[honesty=sly] : For a penny. | Dull? Ask the priest. | Not me. Probably.
b[temper=short] : Use your own. | Sharpen it, then. | Look elsewhere.
b : Go on. | Mine too. | Not me.
a : Thanks. | Ha. | Hm.

scene w7c_closing
when topic=work here.time=dusk|night
a : Shall we shut up shop? | That's enough for one day. | Put the shutters up. I'm done.
b[drive=ambitious] : One more hour. | Never enough. | Not yet.
b[tired=yes] : Please. Yes. Please. | More than enough. | Gladly.
b : Aye. | Aye, it is. | Right.
a : One hour. | Home. | Good.

scene w7c_opening
when topic=work here.time=dawn
a : Shutters up. Another day. | Sweep the step and we're open. | Light the fire, will you? My paws are frozen.
b[tired=yes] : Already? I only just shut them. | My broom's asleep. | I'm frozen too.
b : Another day. | Done. | Done.
a : Another. | Open. | Bless you.

scene w7c_coin
when topic=work
a : Is this coin real? Bite it. | Somebody paid me with a clipped penny. | Look at this. Never seen a coin like it.
b[job=official|merchant] : Clipped. Take it to the official. | It's light. Weigh it. | Foreign. Worth half.
b[stage=young] : Can I keep it? | Can I bite it? | Shiny!
b : Looks real enough. | Clipped? Who? | Foreign, I'd say.
a : I'll bite it. | I wish I knew. | Worth something?

scene w7c_rain_day
when topic=work here.weather=rain|storm
a : Nobody's out in this. Dead day. | Rain's kept them all at home. | Stand by the fire. Nobody's coming.
b[role=merchant] : Dead as a doornail. | Not a soul. | Not one.
b[job=farmer|herder|woodcutter|laborer] : Dead? I'm soaked to the bone, out there. | Lucky them. | Lucky you, indoors.
b : Nice and quiet, then. | Let it rain. | Good.
a : Too quiet. | Let it. | Warm.

scene w7c_fog_day
when topic=work here.weather=fog
a : Can't see the end of my own nose. | Fog's so thick I walked into the wall. | Lost the street in this.
b[humour=merry] : Your nose is long. Good. | The wall started it. | Follow your nose.
b : Mind yourself. | Ouch. | Wait for it to lift.
a : I am. | Ouch. | I'll wait.

scene w7c_hot_day
when topic=work here.weather=clear here.season=summer
a : Too hot to think. | My fur's a blanket in this. | Is there any water left?
b[job=smith|baker|cook] : Too hot? Come and stand at my fire. | Shed it. | Drink mine.
b : Sit in the shade. | Shear it off. | A little.
a : No shade. | Ha. | Thanks.

scene w7c_snow_day
when topic=work here.weather=snow
a : Snowed in the path again. | My paws are blocks of ice. | Nobody's buying in this.
b[job=woodcutter] : They'll buy firewood. | Wrap them. | Wood. They're buying wood.
b : Shovel it. | Warm them by the fire. | Cold keeps them home.
a : I did. Twice. | Thanks. | Wood. Lucky you.

scene w7c_crowd_busy
when topic=work here.crowd=crowd
a : Who are all these folk? | Can't move in here. | Somebody tell them to queue.
b[role=merchant] : Customers! Bless every one. | Good. Busy is good. | Queue? They'll walk.
b[temper=short] : Too many. Out! | Move, then. | Queue!
b : Busy day. | Squeeze through. | They never queue.
a : Too busy. | I'll try. | Never.

scene w7c_crowd_quiet
when topic=work here.crowd=quiet
a : Quiet today. | Not a soul. | You could hear a pin drop.
b[role=merchant] : Too quiet. | Not a sale, either. | Drop a coin. I'd hear that.
b : Nice, for once. | Rest, then. | Peaceful.
a : For once. | Rest. | Very.

scene w7c_good_tool
when topic=work
a : Look at this. New. Finest I've ever owned. | Bought myself a proper set at last. | Feel the balance on that.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Must have cost a fortune. | Lucky you. | Lovely. I'll never own one.
b[stage=old] : Look after it and it'll see you out. | Proper tools, proper work. | Balanced. Nice.
b : Lovely. | About time. | Nice weight.
a : It did. | About time. | Lovely.

scene w7c_burnt
when topic=work
a : Burnt my paw on it. | Ow. Ow ow ow. | Don't touch that. Hot.
b[job=healer] : Cold water. Now. Don't argue. | Let me see. | Thanks for the warning.
b[humour=merry] : That'll teach you. | Kiss it better? | Too late!
b : Cold water. | Ouch. | Thanks.
a : Ow. | Ouch. | Hot.

scene w7c_tidy
when topic=work
a : Who left this mess? | You could tidy, you know. | Somebody's been at my bench.
b[honesty=frank] : Me. Sorry. | I could. I won't. | I borrowed your bench. Sorry.
b[honesty=sly] : Rats. | Could I? | Rats again.
b : Not me. | I'll tidy later. | Not me.
a : Somebody. | Later. | Somebody.

scene w7c_stranger_ask_work
when topic=work|smalltalk pair.band=strangers a.wealth=poor|destitute
a : Any work going? I'll do anything. | Does your master need a pair of paws? | I'm new in town. Know anyone hiring?
b[warmth=warm] : Ask at the yard. Tell them I sent you. | I'll ask. Come back tomorrow. | The docks, always. Ask for the foreman.
b[warmth=cold] : No. | Ask him yourself. | No.
b : Try the market. | Not that I know. | Ask at the inn.
a : Thank you. | I'll try. | Thank you.

scene w7c_lunch
when topic=work here.time=day
a : What's in your pail today? | Swap you half? | I've brought too much bread.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Nothing much. | Gladly. | I'll take any.
b[wealth=rich] : Cold pie. Have some. | Swap? Have it. | Bread? I've cheese.
b : Bread and onion. | Half's fair. | Share it.
a : Same. | Half. | Here.

## ---------------------------------------------------------------- Still more of the everyday, for anyone at work

scene w7c_boots
when topic=work
a : My boots have gone through at the toe. | Look at this coat. More patch than coat. | I've worn a hole in my apron the shape of my belly.
b[wealth=rich] : Buy new, for pity's sake. | Get a proper one made. I'll tell you who. | Well, it's a handsome belly.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Stuff them with straw. Mine are. | Patches are honest. | Turn it round. Wear the back.
b[job=crafter] : Bring them by. I'll do it at cost. | I can fix that. Restday. | Leave it with me.
b : Get them mended. | Patch the patches. | Ha! So you have.
a : Next month. | I will. | Laugh, go on.

scene w7c_mouser
when topic=work
a : The cat caught three rats in the store last night. | Somebody's been feeding the yard cat. It's useless now. | There's a dog sleeping on the sacks again.
b[warmth=warm] : Good cat. Give it a bit of something. | Me. Sorry. It looked so thin. | Let it sleep. It's cold out.
b[temper=short] : Good. Now catch the rest. | Stop it, whoever it is. | Kick it off.
b : Earns its keep, that one. | Fat cats don't hunt. | Shoo it off.
a : Better than some of us. | They don't. | It won't shoo.

scene w7c_wasp
when topic=work here.season=summer|autumn
a : There's a wasp in here. Where'd it go? | Something stung me! | Don't move. It's on your ear.
b[temper=nervy] : Where? Where? Get it out! | Ow! Me too! | Get it off. Get it off!
b[humour=merry] : It's behind you. No, the other behind. | Rub dock leaf on it and cry. | It likes you.
b : Open the door. | Show me. | ...Has it gone?
a : It's gone. I think. | Here. Swelling. | Gone.

scene w7c_read_order
when topic=work
a : Can you read this? Somebody's left an order. | What does this word say? | My letters are poor. Read me this.
b[job=scholar|official|priest] : Of course. "Twelve, by Restday, and no excuses." | That says "urgent". It's underlined. | Give it here. Hm. Rude, but clear.
b[talk=quiet] : ...Sorry. I can't. | I don't know. | No.
b : Twelve of something, by Restday. | "Urgent", I think. | Something about pay.
a : Twelve! | Lovely. | Pay? Good.

scene w7c_measure
when topic=work
a : It's too short. I measured it twice! | Who cut this? It's crooked as a dog's leg. | It doesn't fit. Nothing fits today.
b[temper=short] : Then measure three times. | Not me. | Make it fit.
b[humour=dry] : Twice wrong, then. | A crooked dog, by the look. | Nothing ever fits. That's the trade.
b : Start again. | Ask who had the saw. | Shave a bit off.
a : I'll start again. | Nobody owns up. | Fine.

scene w7c_late_delivery
when topic=work
a : The delivery's late again. | Where's that cart? It said dawn. | I've nothing to work with till it comes.
b[job=carter] : Don't look at me. Mine's on time. Mostly. | The north road's half mud. | Sit tight. They're coming.
b[temper=short] : Then shout at the carter. | Dawn where? | Find something.
b : It'll come. | Bad roads. | Sweep, then.
a : When? | Always. | Sweep. Lovely.

scene w7c_payday_plans
when topic=work a.shift=during|after
a : What'll you do with your #wages#? | Paid tomorrow. I've spent it already, in my head. | One more day to pay.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Rent. Then nothing. | So have I. On rent. | It'll be gone by the next day.
b[humour=merry] : Ale. Then more ale. Then soup. | On what? Tell me. | One more day of being poor.
b[drive=ambitious] : Save it. Every penny. | I'm putting it by for a stall. | Spend it on a better tool.
b : Pay what I owe. | Same. | Hold on.
a : Sensible. | Same. | Hold on.

scene w7c_saving
when topic=work a.stage=adolescent|adult
a : I'm saving for a good coat. | Six more months and I'll have enough for a stall. | I'm putting by a penny a day. For the wedding.
b[warmth=warm] : Good for you! I'll help you choose. | You'll get there. | A wedding! Whose?
b[honesty=sly] : Keep it under the floor. Not in the house. | A stall? Mine's for sale. | A penny a day? Lend me one.
b : Good. | Six months goes quick. | Whose wedding?
a : Thank you. | I hope. | Mine. Maybe.

scene w7c_own_shop
when topic=work a.drive=ambitious|restless
a : One day, my own name over a door. | I'll not work for another wolf forever. | When I'm my own master, I'll do it properly.
b[drive=content] : Why? It's a bother. Let others worry. | I like working for someone. Less to fret over. | Properly's hard.
b[stage=old] : I said that. Forty years ago. | Save first. Then dream. | We'll see.
b : Good. | Go on, then. | Will you?
a : You'll see. | Watch me. | I will.

scene w7c_shop_closing
when topic=work
a : Did you hear the chandler's shutting? | They say the old bakery's closing for good. | Another shop boarded on our street.
b[business=failing] : That'll be me soon. | Don't. I'm next. | Next week, mine.
b[role=merchant] : Their customers'll come to me. | Good. Less competition. Sorry. | Shame. Good spot, too.
b : Shame. | Twenty years they had it. | Hard times.
a : Shame. | Twenty. | Hard.

scene w7c_weights
when topic=work
a : The official's coming round to check the weights. | They're testing scales today. Is yours honest? | Somebody was fined for short weight.
b[honesty=sly] : Mine's honest. Very honest. Let me just adjust it. | As honest as anyone's. | Unlucky.
b[honesty=frank] : Let them. I've nothing to hide. | Always. | Good. Serves them right.
b : Let them. | Course. | Who?
a : Good. | Good. | The one on the corner.

scene w7c_pickpocket
when topic=work here.place=market|street
a : Watch your purse. There's a light paw about. | Saw a pup lift a purse just now. Quick as a fish. | Somebody's been at my takings.
b[role=guard] : Point them out. | Which way did they go? | I'll watch your stall.
b[honesty=sly] : I saw nothing. | Clever pup. | Not me.
b : Thanks for the warning. | Where? | Lock it away.
a : Keep it close. | Gone. | I will.

scene w7c_lend_coin
when topic=work pair.band=acquaintances|friends
a : Lend me a penny till Restday? | Could you spare a few coppers? | I'm short. Just this week.
b[wealth=rich] : Here. Don't worry about it. | A few? Here's more. | Take it.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : I've less than you. | Spare? Ha. | Me too.
b[honesty=guarded] : What for? | For what? | Again?
b : Restday. Promise? | Here. | Just this week.
a : Promise. | Bless you. | Just this week.

scene w7c_old_tool
when topic=work
a : This hammer was my grandfather's. | Old tool, this. Older than me. | The handle's been changed five times. The head never.
b[stage=old] : They made them proper then. | Like me. | Same as my axe.
b : Still works. | Look after it. | Then is it the same hammer?
a : Better than new. | I will. | ...Don't.

scene w7c_pups_underfoot
when topic=work a.parent=yes
a : The pups were underfoot all morning. | Mine wants to help. Helping is worse. | Brought the little one. Couldn't leave her.
b[stage=young] : I'm not underfoot! I'm helping! | I can help! | Hello!
b[warmth=warm] : Let them. They learn by watching. | Give them a broom. | She's welcome.
b[temper=short] : Keep them clear of the fire. | Send them home. | Mind she doesn't touch anything.
b : They're quick, at that age. | It's sweet. | Fair enough.
a : Too quick. | It's slow. | She's good.

scene w7c_caught_napping
when topic=work
a : Were you asleep? | Wake up! | You're snoring on the job.
b[tired=yes] : I was resting my eyes. Hard. | I'm awake. I'm awake. | Only a little.
b[humour=merry] : Thinking. Deeply. | I was listening to the wood grow. | Snoring's a kind of singing.
b : No. | I'm up! | Was I?
a : Hm. | Good. | Loudly.

scene w7c_customer_gossip
when topic=work
a : A customer told me the strangest thing today. | You hear everything behind a counter. | Old so-and-so came in. Talked an hour.
b[talk=chatty] : What? Tell me! | Tell me everything. | Talked! About what?
b[honesty=guarded] : Best not repeat it. | Then keep it there. | Did they buy anything?
b : Oh? | I bet. | Did they buy?
a : I'll tell you later. | It's true. | A button.

scene w7c_steward
when topic=work a.house
a : The House steward came round with his ledger. | Steward's counted every nail in the yard. | They want the accounts by Restday.
b[self.house] : Ours too. Counted twice. | He's always counting. | Again?
b : Did he find anything? | Every nail? | Restday!
a : Nothing. This time. | Every one. | Restday.

scene w7c_other_towns
when topic=work
a : In Larkfield, they say, a stall pays twice what it does here. | Ridgemere work pays better, I'm told. | Southmeadow folk work half as hard. All that sun.
b[from=larkfield] : True. And the rent's three times. | So I'm told. | We work in the sun!
b[from=southmeadow] : Half as hard? We work twice as long. | Ridgemere pays. Ridgemere charges. | Come and pick apples and say that.
b[from=frosthollow] : Try a day in the mines. Then tell me who works. | Pays more, costs more. | Sun's lovely. Try snow.
b[from=ridgemere] : And costs double. | It does. Ask anyone. | Half as hard. Twice as happy.
b : They say a lot. | Is it? | I've heard.
a : They do. | I've heard. | They do.

scene w7c_lamp_oil
when topic=work here.time=dusk|night
a : Lamp oil's half gone already. | Can't see a thing. More light! | My eyes are going in this light.
b[wealth=poor|destitute] : Work in the dark. I do. | Light costs. | Mine went years ago.
b : Fill it, then. | Here. | Rest them.
a : With what? | Thanks. | I'll try.

scene w7c_big_job_done
when topic=work
a : Done! The big one's done! | Finished it. Three weeks I've been at it. | It's done. Come and look.
b[warmth=warm] : Oh, it's beautiful! Well done! | Three weeks! You must be proud. | Show me!
b[warmth=cold] : About time. | Took you long enough. | I'll look later.
b[humour=merry] : Let's drink to it! | Three weeks? I'd have done it in two. | Ooh!
b : Well done. | At last. | Let's see.
a : Thank you. | At last. | There.

scene w7c_charm
when topic=work
a : Where's my lucky stone? I always work with it on the bench. | I touched wood this morning and still dropped everything. | My lucky nail's gone missing.
b[piety=devout] : Pray. Stones don't listen. | The gods don't need wood. | Trust in the gods, not nails.
b[humour=dry] : It's lucky somewhere else now. | Should've touched more wood. | A nail can't be lucky. It's a nail.
b : Under the bench? | Bad luck. | It'll turn up.
a : Not there. | Very bad. | Hope so.

scene w7c_teach_me
when topic=work pair.band=acquaintances|friends|strangers
a : Could you teach me your trade? | How long did it take you to learn that? | Would you take an apprentice?
b[master=yes] : I've one already. One's plenty. | Years. Still learning. | I've one. Ask me in a year.
b[warmth=warm] : I could show you a little. Come by. | Years. But you'd be quicker. | Maybe. Come and watch.
b[warmth=cold] : No. | Too long for you. | No.
b : It's not easy. | Years. | Perhaps.
a : I'm a quick learner. | Years! | Perhaps.

scene w7c_mud
when topic=work here.weather=rain|storm|snow
a : Who tracked mud all through? | Wipe your paws! | The floor's a pig-sty.
b[humour=merry] : Mud's free. Enjoy it. | They don't wipe. Nobody wipes. | Oink.
b : Customers. | Sorry. | I'll sweep.
a : Customers. | Wipe them. | Please.

scene w7c_quiet_moment
when topic=work
a : Listen. Nothing. Lovely. | This is the best part of the day. The quiet part. | I like it when it's just us.
b[talk=chatty] : Isn't it? Now, did I tell you... | It is. Let me tell you why. | Me too! Now then...
b : Lovely. | It is. | Me too.
a : ...It was. | It is. | Mm.

scene w7c_wrong_order
when topic=work
a : They ordered blue. I made blue. Now they want green. | Customer changed his mind. Again. | They wanted it smaller. After I'd finished.
b[temper=short] : Charge them double. | Throw it at him. | Tell them no.
b[humour=dry] : Make it blue-green. Everyone loses. | His mind's like the weather. | Cut it in half. Two small ones.
b : Customers. | Typical. | Charge for it.
a : Customers. | Every time. | I will.

scene w7c_good_customer
when topic=work
a : A customer paid me extra. Just because. | Somebody said my work was the best in town. | Old dear brought me a pie for mending her chair.
b[warmth=warm] : Oh, that's lovely. You deserve it. | You are, you know. | Bless her.
b[honesty=sly] : Did they? I'll send them more of mine. | Who? I'll pay them to say it of me. | Share the pie?
b : That's rare. | Nice. | That's kind.
a : Rare as hen's teeth. | It was. | It was.

scene w7c_thief_tools
when topic=work
a : Somebody stole my best saw. | Lost a whole morning looking for my mallet. | Tools keep walking off.
b[role=guard] : Report it. We'll look. | Lock them up. | I'll ask about.
b[honesty=sly] : Walking off? Funny that. | Look in the river. | Tools have legs.
b : Lock them up. | Found it? | Thieves.
a : I will. | No. | Thieves.

scene w7c_sore_back
when topic=work a.stage=adult|old
a : My back's not right. | Bent over all day. I'll be crooked as a crook. | I creak when I stand.
b[job=healer] : Warm stones on it tonight. | Lie flat. Not soft. Flat. | Come and see me.
b[stage=old] : Wait till it's every day. | Mine's been crooked for years. | Me too.
b : Stretch it. | Stand up straight now and then. | Rest it.
a : I'll try. | Easy said. | I'll try.
